  VdiConfBrokerRestart   = "{0}: the services Tssdis, TScPubRPC and RDMS stop and start again, Tssdis first (about a minute; one that hangs has its process ended), then the Kerberos tickets of NETWORK SERVICE are purged.`r`n`r`nSessions already open are not touched. Meanwhile {1} serves the new sign-ins."
  VdiConfPurge           = "{0}: the Kerberos tickets of NETWORK SERVICE, the account of the broker services, are purged. The broker asks for new ones at its next request: nothing stops, nobody is signed out."
  VdiConfRepair          = "{0}: the task '{1}' is installed (or updated). It restarts the broker services by itself when the broker presents itself without the `$ (the fault that fails every sign-in), at most once every 15 minutes.`r`n`r`nThe script goes to C:\ProgramData\OpenThinRDP; nothing else changes."
  VdiConfAddToGroup      = "{0} goes into the AD group {1} (a change in Active Directory), then its Kerberos tickets are purged so that the group counts at once.`r`n`r`nThe hosts give their permissions to that group: this is how the broker gets them."
  VdiConfPerm            = "On {0}, {1} goes into: {2}.`r`nThen the Kerberos tickets of the brokers ({3}) are purged, so that the permissions count at the next sign-in.`r`n`r`nNo VM, service or session is touched."
  VdiConfUnblock         = "{0}: the RDVH agent (VmHostAgent) stops with a time limit, its process is ended if it hangs, and it starts again.`r`n`r`nThe VMs keep running and open sessions are not touched; for about a minute the desktops of this host do not start on demand."
  VdiConfUnblockVmms     = "{0}: the Hyper-V management service (vmms) stops with a time limit, its process is ended if it hangs, and it starts again.`r`n`r`nThe VMs keep running (each in its own process); for about a minute nobody can start, stop or sign in to a desktop of this host."
